# Astro and Svelte Integration

This rule describes how Astro and Svelte are integrated in the AgriFlow project.

## Page Structure

- [src/pages/](mdc:src/pages) - Contains all Astro pages
- [src/layouts/](mdc:src/layouts) - Contains reusable layouts

## Astro with Svelte

Astro is used as the main framework for static rendering, while Svelte is used for interactive components.

### Best Practices

- Use Astro for static content
- Use Svelte for interactive UI parts
- Partial hydration with `client:load` or `client:visible` directives for Svelte components
- Pass data from Astro components to Svelte components via props

### Integration Example

```astro
---
// Astro Page
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Counter from '../components/ui/Counter.svelte';

const pageTitle = "Integration Example";
const initialCount = 0;
---

<MainLayout title={pageTitle}>
  <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
  
  <div class="static-content">
    <p>Static content rendered by Astro</p>
  </div>
  
  <div class="interactive-component">
    <!-- Client-side hydration of Svelte component -->
    <Counter client:load initialCount={initialCount} />
  </div>
</MainLayout>
```

## Routing

- Routing is handled by Astro via the file structure in `src/pages/`
- Dynamic routes use the `[param].astro` format
- API routes are defined in `src/pages/api/`
